{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Analysis.Convex.Deriv","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.LobachevskyDerivative","lean:module:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity"],"declarations":18,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_maximiser_unique","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart_maximiser_unique","kind":"theorem","line":358,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L358-L364","doc":"**At most one maximiser.**  The immediate consequence, and the shape\n`qou-krvm` needs on the polytope (there, for the polytope's own functional --\nsee the header: this is the single-tetrahedron simplex, not that polytope). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.octahedral_mem_angleSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.octahedral_mem_angleSimplex","kind":"theorem","line":352,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L352-L356","doc":"The octahedral shape `(π/2, π/4, π/4)` — the L6a4 symmetric point, and the\n`q → 1` Descartes shape — lies in the open simplex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.regular_mem_angleSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.regular_mem_angleSimplex","kind":"theorem","line":347,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L347-L350","doc":"The regular ideal tetrahedron `(π/3, π/3, π/3)` lies in the open simplex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.strictConcaveOn_volChart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.strictConcaveOn_volChart","kind":"theorem","line":289,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L289-L339","doc":"**T3 — the Lobachevsky volume sum is strictly concave on the open angle\nsimplex.**\n\nProved by restricting to an arbitrary segment and applying Mathlib's\n`strictConcaveOn_of_deriv2_neg` to the restriction, whose second derivative is\nthe `hessian_neg_definite` quadratic form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.deriv2_volSeg_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.deriv2_volSeg_neg","kind":"theorem","line":260,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L260-L283","doc":"**The second derivative is negative** whenever the direction is nonzero.\n\nThis is the step that reuses `hessian_neg_definite`: after `w = -u - v` is\nsubstituted, the three `Λ''` terms ARE its quadratic form. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hasDerivAt_dvolSeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hasDerivAt_dvolSeg","kind":"theorem","line":194,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L194-L258","doc":"**Second derivative of the restriction**, via T1's `Λ'' = -cot`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.deriv_volSeg_eventuallyEq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.deriv_volSeg_eventuallyEq","kind":"theorem","line":188,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L188-L192","doc":"`deriv (volSeg ...)` agrees with the closed form near any good parameter. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hasDerivAt_volSeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.hasDerivAt_volSeg","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L174-L186","doc":"**First derivative of the restriction.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.segSet_lt_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.segSet_lt_pi","kind":"theorem","line":167,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L167-L172","doc":"Each angle is `< π` on `segSet`, because the three sum to `π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.dvolSeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.dvolSeg","kind":"def","line":159,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L159-L163","doc":"The closed form of its first derivative (`Λ' = -log(2 sin ·)`, T1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volSeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volSeg","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L155-L157","doc":"The volume along the segment. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.segSet_isOpen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.segSet_isOpen","kind":"theorem","line":145,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L145-L153","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.segSet","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.segSet","kind":"def","line":140,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L140-L143","doc":"The parameters at which the segment's three angles are all positive.  Since\nthey sum to `π`, positivity of all three already forces each to be `< π`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofChart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.AngleTriple.ofChart","kind":"def","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L124-L132","doc":"The `AngleTriple` at a point of the open simplex. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.mem_angleSimplex_lt_pi","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.mem_angleSimplex_lt_pi","kind":"theorem","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L118-L122","doc":"A point of the simplex has all three angles in `(0, π)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.angleSimplex_convex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.angleSimplex_convex","kind":"theorem","line":107,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L107-L116","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.volChart","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L72-L77","doc":"**The volume functional in the chart**, DEFINED as the Lobachevsky sum.\n\nA definition, not the geometric volume: identifying it with the hyperbolic\nvolume of the ideal tetrahedron is `qou-idvt` T2, which is open. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.angleSimplex","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Archimedean.IdealTetrahedronConcavity.angleSimplex","kind":"def","line":67,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Archimedean/IdealTetrahedronVolumeConcavity.lean#L67-L70","doc":"**The open angle simplex, in the `(alpha, beta)` chart.**\n`gamma = pi - alpha - beta` is then automatically positive. ","signatureChunk":0}]}